-------------------------------------------------------------------------------
1. Definitions
-------------------------------------------------------------------------------

"Software" means the Migo mini-game runtime as Licensor makes it available in
object-code form -- including libraries, frameworks, Android archives (AAR) and
Swift packages -- together with the C ABI headers, interface definitions, host
integration source code (such as the Linux Qt 6 host kit and the OpenHarmony
host project), sample code and documentation that accompany it, and any update
Licensor makes available under this License. The Software does not include the
source code of the runtime engine, and nothing in this License grants any right
to it.

"You" means the individual or legal entity exercising rights under this
License, together with its Affiliates.

"Affiliate" means any entity that controls, is controlled by, or is under common
control with an entity, where "control" means ownership of more than fifty
percent of the voting interests or the power to direct its management.

"Your App" means an application that You own and control and that is
distributed to End Users primarily to provide Your own application
functionality, and not primarily to provide a mini-game runtime, engine or SDK.

"End User" means a person who obtains Your App to use it, and not to build
products from the Software.

"Production Use" means making the Software available to End Users, or using it
to serve End Users, in any form other than for internal development, testing or
evaluation.

"Small Entity" means an entity that, together with its Affiliates, satisfies
both of the following as of its most recently completed fiscal year:
  (a) total annual gross revenue, from all sources and not only from Your App,
      of no more than USD 1,000,000 (or the equivalent in another currency);
      AND
  (b) no more than 3,000,000 monthly active users across all instances of Your
      App in any single month of that year.

"Competitive Offering" means any product or service (including a hosted or
managed service) that:
  (a) is a mini-game runtime, mini-game engine, or mini-game hosting/runtime
      SDK substantially similar to the Software; AND
  (b) is provided, licensed, distributed, sold, made available, or otherwise
      offered to any third party as a standalone product/service, or as a
      component whose primary purpose is to enable third parties to run
      mini-games.
  Without limiting the foregoing, a Competitive Offering includes:
    1) distributing the Software, or any part of it, as a standalone SDK,
       engine, library, framework or toolkit, whether or not bundled with
       other code;
    2) offering to third parties a hosted, cloud or managed mini-game
       runtime/engine service whose core runtime functionality is provided by
       the Software; and
    3) rebranding or repackaging the Software as a new mini-game engine
       product for provision to third parties.

-------------------------------------------------------------------------------
2. License Grants
-------------------------------------------------------------------------------

Subject to Your compliance with this License, Licensor grants You a worldwide,
non-exclusive, non-transferable, non-sublicensable, royalty-free license to:

2.1 Development and evaluation. Install, copy and use the Software internally,
    at any scale, to develop, build, test, evaluate and benchmark Your App and
    mini-games, and to evaluate the Software itself. The Small Entity
    thresholds do not apply to this Section 2.1.

2.2 Production Use by Small Entities. While You are a Small Entity, embed the
    Software in Your App and distribute it to End Users solely as part of Your
    App, for the purpose of running mini-games within Your App. If You cease to
    be a Small Entity, this Section 2.2 continues to cover Your existing
    Production Use for ninety (90) days, so that You can obtain a commercial
    license without interrupting Your service.

2.3 Headers, host integration code and samples. Copy, modify and compile the
    header files, interface definitions, host integration source code and
    sample code included in the Software, solely as needed to integrate the
    Software into Your App, and distribute the result as part of Your App under
    Section 2.2 or a commercial license.

2.4 Packaging. Strip, sign, compress and split the Software's binaries, and
    place them in delivery modules or in storage You control, solely as needed
    to deliver the Software into Your App. Delivering the Software into Your App
    on demand -- for example through a Play Feature Delivery module, or from
    storage You control on stores that offer no such mechanism -- is
    distribution as part of Your App, provided that the endpoint serves only
    the delivery of Your App and that You do not present the hosted file as an
    SDK, a library or a general-purpose runtime download.

2.5 Mini-games. Develop, publish, distribute and sell mini-games that run on
    the Software, whether authored by You or by third parties. Running
    third-party mini-games inside Your App -- including operating a mini-game
    platform within Your App and giving game developers tools and documentation
    to target it -- is use within Your App, provided that the Software itself
    stays embedded in Your App and is not provided to those developers.

2.6 Benchmarks. Publish the results of benchmarks of the Software, provided
    that You disclose the versions, devices and methodology used.

Any Production Use not covered by Section 2.2 requires a separate written
commercial license from Licensor. Contact: licensing@minigame-labs.com.

